    <h2>About reviews on this page</h2>
    <p>
      We only publish testimonials from real sellers who gave us permission to use them,
      and we don't publish an aggregate star rating until there are enough verified reviews
      to make one meaningful. Sites that show a 4.9 out of 247 reviews on day one didn't
      earn them.
    </p>
    <p>
      The same rule applies to closed deals. Where a house wasn't in Gaston, Cleveland or
      Lincoln County, we say so on the entry rather than letting you assume otherwise. A
      buyer who quietly presents an out-of-area deal as local is telling you something about
      how they'll handle your house.
    </p>
    <p>
      Agent reviews are held to a third rule. They come from public third-party profiles
      rather than being given to us privately, so every one is quoted with the platform named
      and a link to the original, go and read it there. A review you cannot go and
      check is a claim, and we would rather hand you the link than ask you to take our word
      for it.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

